cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article that
  introduces the protocol.
title: "treatment-identity: verify that the treatment an experiment declares is the one its data loader delivers"
abstract: >-
  Five CPU treatment-delivery gates probe what a data loader returns at the
  training-step-input boundary rather than what its configuration requests. A
  separate geometry gate checks evaluation integrity. The six checks run
  against synthetic fixtures in seconds, before any GPU budget is committed,
  and fail on unexpected equality as well as unexpected difference. Their
  certificates are bounded observations and do not attest optimiser
  consumption or optimisation correctness.
type: software
